{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00337","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00337@rel:R25-11#197d8662","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00337","release":"R25-11","content":"function RecoverFile [SWS_PER_00337] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; RecoverFile ( ara::core::StringView fileName) noexcept; Recovers a file of this File Storage. This method allows to recover a single file when the redundancy checks fail. It will fail with kResourceBusy when the file is currently open. This method does a best-effort recovery of the file. After recovery, the file might show outdated or initial content, or might be lost. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::FileStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kPhysical no_rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fileName td File name of the file. May correspond to the PersistencyFile.file Name of a configured file. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td StorageFailure td Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption or decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if the file is open, or if DeleteFile or ResetFile with the same file name is currently being executed. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the recovered file. td PerErrc ::kFileNotFound td rollback_semantics Returned if the provided file does not exist in the File Storage. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the recovered file would exceed the configured maximumAllowedSize of the File Storage. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating or checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00337","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"RecoverFile","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_FileStorage_29266b.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1},"evidence":{"figures":[],"snippets":[{"id":"SNIP_per_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_P_P126_391","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Persistency","p":126,"rel":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE (deterministic citation)","n":9,"x":"c (RS_PER_00001, RS_PER_00004, RS_AP_00119, RS_AP_00120, RS_AP_00121, RS_AP_00127, RS_AP_00132, RS_AP_00135, RS_AP_00139) 8.3.11.7 FileStorage::RecoverFile [SWS_PER_00337] Definition of API function…","src":"snippet"},{"id":"SNIP_per_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_P_P20_42","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Persistency","p":20,"rel":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE (deterministic citation)","n":84,"x":"[SWS_PER_00042] [SWS_PER_00043] [SWS_PER_00044] [SWS_PER_00046] [SWS_PER_00047] [SWS_PER_00048] [SWS_PER_00049] [SWS_PER_00